  <data name="cbOptimize.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>None - nothing is optimized
Basic - only unreferenced procedures and variables will be removed
Full - more optimization like constant folding, dead code removal, variable combine
Experimental - even more optimization (variable reuse, constant propagation) - breaks code
in some cases, use Full instead</value>
  </data>
  <data name="cbShortCircuit.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When script is compiled with this option enabled, 
right-side of all AND, OR expressions will not be evaluated
in case result is already known. Examples:

(X and Y) - if X is false, Y will not be evaluated (result is false)
(X or Y) - if X is true, likewise Y will be skipped (result is true)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="cbAutocomplete.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable displaying box with a list of suggested procedure names, 
variables, constants and macros as you type.
Showing the autocompletion box is performed by keyboard shortcut [Ctrl + Space]
(required program restart)</value>
  </data>
